    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d242">

                <pb facs="0445" n="345" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg345"/>

                <head>No. 242.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Morgan to Mr. Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-01-02"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 2, 1884.</date>
                        (Received January 22.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 738.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In obedience to the instructions contained
                    in your No. 470, 15th November, 1883, I addressed a note to Señor Fernandez on
                    the 8th of December last, in which I again called his attention to the claim of
                    the owners of the schooner Daylight, by reason of the sinking of that vessel by
                    the Independencia, a Mexican national vessel.</p>
                <p>Señor Fernandez has not replied to my note, and I deem it proper to let you see
                    that your instructions have been carried out.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>P. H. MORGAN.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d242-a1.xml" xpointer="d242-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
